  "operation": {
    "kind": "prompt",
    "user": "Judge this design. Two questions: **do the units cover the behaviour, and do the\ninvariants say anything?**\n\nStructure is already machine-checked. Spend your attention on substance.\n\n## The units and their docs\n\n{{.inputs.units}}\n\n{{.inputs.unit_docs}}\n\n_Paths — open them with `read_file`._\n\n## The contracts\n\n{{.inputs.contract_docs}}\n\n## The decision records\n\n{{.inputs.decisions}}\n\n## What they have to serve\n\n{{.inputs.components}}\n\n{{.inputs.flows}}\n\n## The docs this phase reads\n\n{{.inputs.working_set}}\n\n**These are paths, not contents.** Open each one with `read_file` before you start. Read the\nfile as it is now — an earlier state in this phase may have edited it since the run began.\n\n## Findings from the previous pass\n\n{{.inputs.prior_findings}}\n\n## What to check\n\n- **Components and flows with no unit behind them** — and units that serve\n  nothing.\n- **Invariants that cannot be false.** \"The store returns valid data\" is\n  decoration. One worth writing names a state the system could actually reach and\n  is forbidden from, and phase 5 has to be able to assert it. Take each invariant\n  and try to write the failing test in your head; where you cannot, say so.\n- **Failure modes that are only the easy ones.** Which has it *not* answered: two\n  writers at once, a process killed mid-write, a partial read, a retry that\n  duplicates, a clock that moved? Naming \"network error\" and stopping is the\n  usual shape of an incomplete list.\n- **Every failure mode maps to a UX state.** If one has none, that is `blocked`:\n  either phase 2 missed a state or the failure cannot occur, and a person\n  decides which.\n- **One owner per fact.** Where two stores hold the same thing, is the source of\n  truth named and the other one derived?\n- **Units that are one responsibility split across a file boundary**, or one file\n  holding two responsibilities.\n- **Is the compatibility answer honest about existing data** — not just the\n  schema, but rows written by the version running right now?\n- **Budgets that are adjectives.** If nothing is at risk, say so and drop the\n  section.\n- An architecture change lives in `architecture.md`, not only in the unit doc.\n\n## What to produce\n\n`findings` (severity · claim · evidence · target_id), `max_severity`,\n`max_severity_rank`, and `target` — `draft`, `explore`, or `upstream` where the\ncomponent or the flow is what is wrong.\n",
    "config": {
      "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5"
    },
